# Cloudflare Pages routing — intentionally no rules.
#
# Every public route is prerendered to a real file by scripts/prerender.mjs
# (/company → company.html, /service/service-1 → service/service-1.html), so the
# old catch-all `/* /index.html 200` SPA fallback is no longer needed — and was
# actively harmful: it answered EVERY unknown URL with 200 + the home page's
# <title>, a soft 404 that drove measured title duplication to 100% and burned
# crawl budget. Unmatched paths now fall through to dist/404.html, which
# Cloudflare serves with a genuine 404.
#
# /admin is deliberately NOT mapped here. The CMS needs Postgres, which exists
# on Railway (where Express serves its own SPA fallback) but not on Pages, so on
# this deployment it is correctly a 404 rather than a shell that cannot load.
# Note a rewrite to /index.html would 308 anyway — Pages normalises "/index".
